---
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Consulting and advisory · Aaron Amerling"
	description="Fractional and advisory work for founders and growth-stage teams. Marketing strategy and systems first, then AI and automation layered on top."
>
	<div class="wrap section-lg prose">
		<p class="eyebrow reveal">Advisory and fractional</p>
		<h1 class="reveal">Build the marketing before you automate it.</h1>
		<p class="reveal">
			Most AI marketing programs fail for a boring reason. They automate a funnel that was already
			broken, and now it is broken faster and at greater volume. The strategy and the system have to
			be right first. Then the automation is worth wiring together.
		</p>

		<h2 class="reveal">What I work on</h2>
		<ul class="reveal">
			<li>Performance marketing and demand generation</li>
			<li>Go-to-market and positioning</li>
			<li>
				Answer engine and generative engine optimization, getting cited inside AI answers, not just
				ranked in a list. I built this as a working channel before the category had a name.
			</li>
			<li>Marketing systems and automation architecture, full-funnel pipelines built hands-on, not briefed out.</li>
			<li>Marketing organization design, structure, specialist career paths, insource vs. outsource decisions.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="reveal">How it works</h2>
		<p class="reveal">
			A conversation first, free. Forty-five minutes. If AI or automation is not the thing that will
			move your numbers, I will say so.
		</p>
		<p class="reveal">
			A short diagnostic. Two to three weeks. What is happening in the funnel, where the leverage is,
			and what the sequence should be. You keep the document whether or not we continue.
		</p>
		<p class="reveal">
			Ongoing fractional work. A set number of days a month, running the strategy layer alongside
			your team.
		</p>
		<p class="reveal">I take a small number of engagements at a time.</p>

		<PullQuote quote="My go-to innovator of marketing strategy." name="Sarah Rowlett" roleAtTime="Senior Account Director, TrendSource" current="Account Manager (ex-Google)" />
		<PullQuote quote="An incredibly strategic thinker." name="Jeffrey Tompkins" roleAtTime="Aaron was his client" />

		<h2 class="reveal">Who this is for</h2>
		<p class="reveal">
			Founders and growth-stage teams who have a product that works and a marketing function that
			does not yet match it.
		</p>

		<a class="btn btn-accent reveal" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/?reason=consulting`}>
			Start with a conversation
		</a>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
